# Environment for the BLIS leaderboard.
# Local setup: `set -a; source .env; set +a` (or just use the make targets).
# The image CI reads the dependency refs below; the deployed image overrides the paths.

# --- Dependencies: repo + commit to clone/bundle ---
# Pinned to a known-good TRIPLE. Since blis v0.10.0 (#1851) a deployment is a blis-schemas
# scenario priced by blis-latency-kernel, which resolves hardware + model from a
# blis-catalog clone and coefficient sets from a blis-registry clone. The three co-evolve
# (the kernel's testdata/upstream.lock is authoritative), so bump ALL THREE together, never
# one alone. The catalog MUST match: catalog 0.2.2 adds a hardware field (ComputeCapability)
# that the v0.1.0 kernel rejects, so this pins catalog 0.2.1 even though 0.2.2 exists.
BLIS_REPO=https://github.com/inference-sim/inference-sim
BLIS_REF=f079d103413a5a86f18ca8828ce9d626d592b194            # v0.10.0
BLIS_CATALOG_REPO=https://github.com/inference-sim/blis-catalog
BLIS_CATALOG_REF=28e82d4c249893ee25b1412a63d2347c5165b004    # 0.2.1 (kernel-locked)
BLIS_REGISTRY_REPO=https://github.com/inference-sim/blis-registry
BLIS_REGISTRY_REF=f7519b12b3393851a3ad416e26c819dd951d4c0d   # v0.1.1

# --- Runtime paths: where `leaderboard serve` keeps state ---
BLIS_CATALOG=../blis-catalog     # the blis-catalog clone; required for any run
BLIS_REGISTRY=../blis-registry   # the blis-registry clone; required for any run
LEADERBOARD_RESULTS=results      # results dir, relative to the repo root
# LEADERBOARD_USER_MODELS defaults to <results>/user-models; leave unset locally.
# A deployment moves these to its PVC (e.g. /data/results, /data/blis-catalog,
# /data/user-models), set in deploy/openshift/leaderboard.yaml, not here.

# --- Optional (unset = built-in default) ---
# LEADERBOARD_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=4096   # trace-upload cap, MiB (default ~1 GiB)
# Nav-rail version labels (GET /api/version); auto-detected, set to override:
# LEADERBOARD_VERSION=
# BLIS_VERSION=
# BLIS_CATALOG_VERSION=
